 34CL    27AL(12C,ANG)                 2014BI03                  ENSDF    202609
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 09-Feb-2026)          
 34CL c  2014Bi03: a 40-MeV {+12}C beam was provided from the 14-UD Pelletron   
 34CL2c  accelerator at the Tata Institute of Fundamental Research, Mumbai. The 
 34CL3c  target was 0.50-mg/cm{+2} {+27}Al on 10-mg/cm{+2} Au backing. States of
 34CL4c  {+34}Cl were populated via the {+27}Al({+12}C,|an){+34}Cl heavy-ion    
 34CL5c  reaction and the deexciting |g rays were detected using the Indian     
 34CL6c  National Gamma Array, consisting of 15 Compton-suppressed clover       
 34CL7c  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO), and integrated 
 34CL8c  polarization asymmetry (IPDCO). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray          
 34CL9c  multipolarities, lifetimes from DSAM lineshape analysis, and transition
 34CLAc  strengths. Comparisons with large-basis shell-model calculations.      
 34CL c  1978Ba39: 27-45-MeV {+12}C beams from the Strasbourg tandem            
 34CL2c  accelerator, France, impinged on 350-|mg/cm{+2} Al targets on Ta       
 34CL3c  backings. |g rays were detected using two Ge(Li) detectors. Measured   
 34CL4c  |g|g-coin and |g|g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray multipolarities, 
 34CL5c  and lifetimes using the Recoil Distance Method (RDM). Also measured the
 34CL6c  {+31}P(|a,n|g){+34}Cl reaction.                                        
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL cG E,RI$From 2014Bi03, unless otherwise noted. No uncertainties for E|g   
 34CL2cG are provided in 2014Bi03. Based on the typical uncertainties reported  
 34CL3cG in other work by the authors using the same INGA detector array, the   
 34CL4cG evaluators assume a |DE|g=1 keV for averaging and least-squares        
 34CL5cG fitting. 2014Bi03 Table I provides only statistical uncertainties for  
 34CL6cG I|g. The systematic uncertainties are |?5%, arising from the efficiency
 34CL7cG curve and fits, as communicated by M. Saha Sarkar in an email reply to 
 34CL8cG B. Singh on February 17, 2014. The evaluators have combined the        
 34CL9cG statistical and systematic uncertainties in quadrature.                
 34CL cG M$Deduced by evaluators based on measured |g|g(|q)(DCO) and            
 34CL2cG |g|g(|q)(POL) in 2014Bi03. R{-DCO}(D) is from gating on a known        
 34CL3cG stretched dipole (|DJ=1) transition and R{-DCO}(Q) is from gating on a 
 34CL4cG known stretched quadrupole (|DJ=2) transition. For stretched transition
 34CL5cG with same multipolarity as the gating transition, R{-DCO} value should 
 34CL6cG be very close to unity. For different multipolarities of the gating and
 34CL7cG projected transitions, the R{-DCO} value depends on the angle between  
 34CL8cG the detectors and the amount of mixing present in the mixed            
 34CL9cG multipolarity transition. However, the authors did not specify the     
 34CLAcG expected R{-DCO} values. Based on Fig. 5 in 2014Bi03, the expected     
 34CLBcG R{-DCO}(Q)|?1.0 and R{-DCO}(D)|?2.0 for stretched quadrupole (|DJ=2) or
 34CLCcG unstretched dipole (|DJ=0) transitions; R{-DCO}(Q)|?0.5 and            
 34CLDcG R{-DCO}(D)|?1.0 for stretched dipole (|DJ=1) transitions. A positive   
 34CLEcG POL indicates an electric character, and a negative POL indicates a    
 34CLFcG magnetic character. Twelve multipolarities are assigned in 1978Ba39,   
 34CLGcG which are consistent with the 2014Bi03 assignments.                    
 34CL cG TI$2014Bi03 Table II provides only statistical uncertainties for the |g
 34CL2cG branching ratios. According to the email reply to B. Singh from the    
 34CL3cG corresponding author M. Saha Sarkar on February 17, 2014, the |g       
 34CL4cG branching ratios listed in Table II of 2014Bi03 were measured          
 34CL5cG separately by gating on transitions above the level. The systematic    
 34CL6cG uncertainties for these measurements are |?5%, which arise from the    
 34CL7cG efficiency curve and fits. The evaluators have combined the statistical
 34CL8cG and systematic uncertainties in quadrature. In some cases, the         
 34CL9cG branching ratios differ significantly from those derived from the I|g  
 34CLAcG data in Table I of 2014Bi03. The I|g data in Table I should be         
 34CLBcG considered more reliable, as the authors suggested in their email      
 34CLCcG reply.                                                                 
